<Page title="Privacy policy" section="Legal" path="/privacy/" description="How personal data is handled on The Emirates Guide: no accounts, no tracking cookies, hosting logs, and emails you choose to send us." sources={[{ title: 'Vercel: Privacy policy', url: 'https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy' }, { title: 'UK Information Commissioner’s Office: Lawful basis for processing', url: 'https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/lawful-basis/' }]}>
  <p>This policy explains how personal data is handled when you use The Emirates Guide (theemiratesguide.tourground.com). The site is built to need very little personal data: there are no accounts, no comments, no advertising trackers, no analytics cookies and no third-party scripts.</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller of personal data processed through this site is <a href="https://tourground.com">Tourground</a>, the publisher of The Emirates Guide.</p>
  <h2>What we process, why, and on what basis</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider, Vercel, processes technical request data (such as IP address, time, requested address and browser details) to deliver pages and protect the service against abuse. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in operating a secure website (UK GDPR and GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter sign-ups.</strong> The sign-up form does not send anything to us by itself. It opens an email in your own email app, addressed to us and containing the address you typed. If you send it, we use your email address only to send you the newsletter until you unsubscribe. Legal basis: your consent (Article 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time by replying “unsubscribe” or emailing us.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails you send us.</strong> If you email us, we process your email address, your name if given, and your message, to reply and to handle any correction request. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in answering you.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>We do not sell personal data, share it for behavioural advertising, or use it for automated decision-making.</p>
  <h2>Who receives it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> (hosting), acting as our processor.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong>, acting as our processor, for messages you send us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Vercel is based in the United States. Where personal data is transferred outside the UK or EU, we rely on the safeguards the law provides, such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Hosting logs are kept by Vercel under its own retention periods. Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Correspondence is kept for as long as needed to deal with it.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for access to, correction or deletion of your personal data, object to processing, or withdraw consent, by emailing us. You can also complain to your local data-protection authority; in the UK, that is the Information Commissioner’s Office.</p>
  <h2>Sites we link to</h2>
  <p>Stories link to official sources and to the Tourground directory. Those sites have their own privacy policies, which apply when you visit them.</p>
</Page>
